 "real_documentation_preflight": "real MRT and manifest hashed only; real header lines 1-98 and real CDS ReadMe checked; no real data row sliced",
 "exposure_statement_v003": "Source: whole file read into memory once and hashed; line boundaries found by find(LF). Header: bytes up to and including the 98th LF sliced and split into lines 1-98; every header line blank-stripped and matched as bytes against the dash-separator pattern (header only, K5); lines 10-17 and 30-38 ASCII-decoded and regex-checked. Data lines 99 onward: only bytes 1-41 sliced, before any interpretation; the LF position bounds the slice and decides the boolean \"line has at least 41 bytes\"; bytes >= 42 touched only by the hash and the LF search, never sliced, decoded, stripped, compared, measured or emitted. Bytes 1-11 of every data line blank-stripped and compared with the two target names; only the two target prefixes tokenized; tokens decoded only after their shape regex matched or, for emission, after every condition passed. CDS ReadMe read, hashed, decoded, tag-stripped; lines 144-216 checked. Manifest read, hashed, JSON-parsed in full; only crosscheck_massmodels.reference_distance_texts accessed; its single string compared by float equality with tokens 2-7 of NGC3198, never emitted or printed. Emitted on success only: five literal tokens per target with byte spans, source line, documented units/semantics, check booleans, assumption states. Never emitted: T, the anchor text, any other row, any byte >= 42. On failure: codes and booleans only.",
